Expose per-zone motion state and add a runtime zone mask

The move-result handler collapsed the per-zone array into a bounding box and
threw the rest away, so a UI could only draw one rectangle - and with two
separate moving objects that box covers both plus everything between them.

Keeps the raw bitmap (ivs_zone_hits) for display, and adds a mask
(ivs_zone_enable, 0 = all zones on) that suppresses motion from zones the user
has switched off. Masked zones still appear in the bitmap so the UI can render
them as "seen but ignored"; they simply do not raise motion, which matters
because otherwise masking a busy corner would not stop recordings firing.

ivs-status now also reports grid_x/grid_y/zones so a client can lay the grid
out without hardcoding 4x4, and ivs-set-zones sets the mask at runtime - no
pipeline restart, matching how ivs-set-sensitivity already behaves.

Both bitmaps are uint64, which covers the 52-ROI ceiling (RSS_IVS_MAX_ROI).

